.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# Test *keys*, not the whole test directory. `test/` was ignored wholesale, which
# protected test/keys/arc.key -- a real private key -- but also silently excluded
# anything else placed under test/. Ignore the hazard, not its parent.
test/keys/

# Python bytecode. The ValiMail harness was dropped on 2026-08-09 in favour of
# the rfc-suites framework's RFC 8617 suite (runtime keys, no stored private
# key at all); no Python remains in this repo, but the pattern stays so a
# stray artefact is never committed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Crash dumps. FreeBSD writes <progname>.core into the cwd, so the name follows
# whichever binary died -- build.core, test.core, securearc.core. A single filename
# only ever blocks the crash that has already happened: build.core was listed here
# after one landed in a commit on 2026-07-26, and test.core walked straight past it
# on 2026-07-29 because the failing binary had a different name. Cores are tens of
# megabytes and can hold key material lifted from process memory, so match the
# pattern.
*.core
